## Package: packages/config

- Name: `@chief-mog-officer/config`
- Dependencies: `zod`
- Export validated env config using Zod

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';

const envSchema = z.object({
  NODE_ENV: z.enum(['development', 'production', 'test']).default('development'),
  DATABASE_URL: z.string().url(),
  REDIS_URL: z.string().url(),
  PORT: z.coerce.number().default(3001),
  API_PORT: z.coerce.number().default(3001),
  WEB_PORT: z.coerce.number().default(5173),
});

export type Env = z.infer<typeof envSchema>;
export function loadEnv(): Env { return envSchema.parse(process.env); }
```

## Package: packages/lib

- Name: `@chief-mog-officer/lib`
- Dependencies: `pino`
- Export: logger (pino instance), error classes (AppError, NotFoundError, ValidationError)

## Package: packages/db

- Name: `@chief-mog-officer/db`
- Dependencies: `drizzle-orm`, `postgres` (postgres.js driver), `dotenv`
- DevDependencies: `drizzle-kit`
- Use `drizzle-orm/postgres-js` adapter
- Schema in `src/schema/` — one file per table, re-exported from `src/schema/index.ts`
- Use `pgTable`, `uuid`, `text`, `timestamp`, `pgEnum`, `jsonb`, `real`, `index`
- UUID PKs with `defaultRandom()`
- All tables get `createdAt` default `now()`, most get `updatedAt`
- Add indexes on all foreign key columns
- `drizzle.config.ts` reads DATABASE_URL from env
- `src/seed.ts` — creates one demo user, one demo project, company profile, a couple competitors, a couple opportunities, and one agent run
- `src/index.ts` — exports the db client (drizzle instance) and all schema

Drizzle config:
```typescript
import { defineConfig } from 'drizzle-kit';
export default defineConfig({
  schema: './src/schema/index.ts',
  out: './src/migrations',
  dialect: 'postgresql',
  dbCredentials: { url: process.env.DATABASE_URL! },
});
```

